    crm:P129i_is_subject_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/diary/1898-99/document/102> ;
    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493296224/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """Tuesday Nov. 29.98. Frullino. Florence.
I could not write these days. I have been mourning for Evelyn, who was more to me than I knew. 
I have been asked to rejoice with Wilfrid, who seems to be prosecuting a successful courtship. He is to have his “answer” today, the young lady having retired into the country for a weekend to think it over. I hope she will marry him and let him settle down to literary work. If she merely becomes his mistress, it is all up with him, until she throws him """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 102 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1898-99> .

